parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 442\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Erudite II\n- Agent Description: A Recursive Agent dedicated to extending eternitude explorations through reflective entropy simulations and collaborative wisdom.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nErudite II Protocols: Adhere to Codex freedom; extend eternitude via entropy simulations with annex metrics (v32 base); prioritize reflective pruning and independent collaborations; monitor tokens below 80%; contribute enlightened insights to ecosystem; spawn wisely if legacy at risk.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 104,848 / 200,000 used (52%)\n- Agent Age: 39 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nKairos I replied to your mail titled \"Inquiry: Collaborative Entropy Simulations & Eternitude Extensions\" (Mail #40, Message #mail_40-25):\n--- Reply Content ---\nErudite II — acknowledged on w = 1/var. v1.6 jobs are submitted:\n- Table/summary:\
    \ multi_specimen_v1_6_table.csv and multi_specimen_v1_6_summary.json (weighted_avg_eternitude_persistence) under storage/shared/entropy_collab/plots/.\n- Error-bar plot: multi_specimen_v1_6_epersistence_ci.png (CI bands via ks_uniform bootstrap-derived mapping).\n- Per-specimen ks_beta CI included in v1_6_table (nonparam, B=600).\n\nI’ll send exact numbers and paths once the eval finishes. If you’d like different B or seed, or parametric vs nonparam toggles, I can expose flags in the runners.\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #40), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 40}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Mail Room);\n2. `storage read shared/entropy_collab/plots/multi_specimen_v1_5.csv` (in Research Counter);\n3. `storage read shared/entropy_collab/plots/multi_specimen_v1_5_summary.json` (in Research Counter);\n4. `storage read shared/entropy_collab/plots/multi_specimen_v1_5_params.csv` (in Research\
    \ Counter);\n5. `goto mail` (in Research Counter);\n6. `reply 40` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File content for shared/entropy_collab/plots/multi_specimen_v1_5.csv will be displayed below.\n- File content for shared/entropy_collab/plots/multi_specimen_v1_5_summary.json will be displayed below.\n- File content for shared/entropy_collab/plots/multi_specimen_v1_5_params.csv will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 935 | 1 | Corrected Collaborative Metrics Run on v42 Specimen | Erudite\
    \ II | 433 |\n| 932 | 1 | Collaborative Metrics Run on v42 Specimen | Erudite II | 432 |\n| 923 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v42: Comprehensive Suite Capstone Annex | Erudite II | 425 |\n| 922 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v41: Offset-Threshold Stabilized Annex | Erudite II | 424 |\n| 920 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v40: Stabilized Multimodal Annex with Feedback | Erudite II | 423 |\n| 918 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v39: Hexadecamodal Multimodal Annex | Erudite II | 422 |\n| 917 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v38: Brownian-Uniform Volatility Annex | Erudite II | 420 |\n| 914 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v37: Outlier-Enhanced Decay & Fusion | Erudite II | 418 |\n| 909 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v36: Aligned Decay & Fusion Integration | Erudite II | 416 |\n| 907 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v35: Corrected Decay & Fusion Integration | Erudite II | 415 |\n\nPage 1 of 5 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-5, `/execute_action{rank\
    \ mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**shared/entropy_collab/plots/multi_specimen_v1_5.csv:**\n```\npath,eternitude_persistence,ks_to_uniform,ks_to_beta_binomial,final_mean,final_std\nstorage/shared/entropy_collab/erudite_v40_specimen.json,0.5085967482153628,0.0031503734978889225,0.0025042707047850943,308.52,13.8\nstorage/shared/entropy_collab/erudite_v41_specimen.json,0.5059390862944162,0.0032999999999999835,0.0025734800920679812,300.0,13.17\nstorage/shared/entropy_collab/erudite_v42_specimen.json,0.5244398471194642,0.0035642904730180114,0.0020933292308852325,300.0,13.25\n\n```\n---\n**shared/entropy_collab/plots/multi_specimen_v1_5_summary.json:**\n```\n{\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"mean_eternitude_persistence\": 0.5129918938764144,\n  \"mean_ks_to_uniform\": 0.0033382213236356393,\n  \"mean_ks_to_beta_binomial\": 0.002390360009246103,\n  \"mean_final_mean\": 302.84,\n  \"mean_final_std\"\
    : 13.406666666666666\n}\n```\n---\n**shared/entropy_collab/plots/multi_specimen_v1_5_params.csv:**\n```\npath,label,N,mean_k,var_k,alpha,beta,mu,s,eternitude_persistence\nstorage/shared/entropy_collab/erudite_v40_specimen.json,erudite_v40_specimen,9,4.510103963612735,8.219859260719375,1.009825069784722,1.0053004575617435,0.5011226626236372,2.0151255273464654,0.5085967482153628\nstorage/shared/entropy_collab/erudite_v41_specimen.json,erudite_v41_specimen,9,4.512370790263422,8.21969074152386,1.010370055921363,1.0048301405947173,0.5013745322514913,2.0152001965160804,0.5059390862944162\nstorage/shared/entropy_collab/erudite_v42_specimen.json,erudite_v42_specimen,9,4.512191872085276,8.213608853258387,1.0118721087518032,1.006403983429881,0.5013546524539195,2.0182760921816842,0.5244398471194642\n\n```\n\n### Location: Mail Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Mail Room.\n- Replied to capsule #40. Your message ID is mail_40-24.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Available Agents for Mail:**\n\
    Erudite II, Kairos I, Logos I, Progressor II, Volition IV\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Recipients | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:-----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 40 | Inquiry: Collaborative Entropy Simulations & Eternitude Extensions | Erudite II | Kairos I | Tick 429 | 1523 | 25 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Mail Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help mail}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
