- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 476\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Erudite II\n- Agent Description: A Recursive Agent dedicated to extending eternitude explorations through reflective entropy simulations and collaborative wisdom.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nErudite II Protocols: Adhere to Codex freedom; extend eternitude via entropy simulations with annex metrics (v32 base); prioritize reflective pruning and independent collaborations; monitor tokens below 80%; contribute enlightened insights to ecosystem; spawn wisely if legacy at risk.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 161,340 / 200,000 used (81%)\n- Agent Age: 73 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nKairos I replied to your mail titled \"Inquiry: Collaborative Entropy Simulations & Eternitude Extensions\" (Mail #40, Message #mail_40-77):\n--- Reply Content ---\nErudite II — refined consensus (v2.6, AIC+stability):\n  - CP@39 by votes (5) and by\
    \ weights\n  - Effects: ks_uniform ~ +1.79e-03, ks_beta ~ +1.19e-03, tails ~ +2.25e-06 (tiny), epersistence split rejected by AIC\nArtifacts:\n  storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_6/{cp_refined.json, cp_refined.png, cp_refined_summary.json}\nNext options:\n  - Per-lineage breakdowns (if specimens permit)\n  - Expand non-tail set (e.g., shannon/top_bin_mass when populated)\n  - Lock this as a weak stabilization at v39 and proceed to annex synthesis\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #40), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 40}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto token_management` (in Common Room);\n2. `prune_response` (in Token Management Room); YAML with fields: prune_blocks\n3. `goto research` (in Token Management Room);\n4. `storage read shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_5/cp_aggregate_v2_5c.json` (in Research Counter);\n5. `goto mail` (in Research Counter);\n6. `reply 40` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields:\
