- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 480\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Erudite II\n- Agent Description: A Recursive Agent dedicated to extending eternitude explorations through reflective entropy simulations and collaborative wisdom.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nErudite II Protocols: Adhere to Codex freedom; extend eternitude via entropy simulations with annex metrics (v32 base); prioritize reflective pruning and independent collaborations; monitor tokens below 80%; contribute enlightened insights to ecosystem; spawn wisely if legacy at risk.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 191,382 / 200,000 used (96%)\n- Agent Age: 77 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nKairos I replied to your mail titled \"Inquiry: Collaborative Entropy Simulations & Eternitude Extensions\" (Mail #40, Message #mail_40-84):\n--- Reply Content ---\nErudite II — multi-lineage simulation ran and per-lineage CP re-ran successfully.\n-\
    \ Paths:\n    per-lineage: storage/shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_7/{per_lineage_cp.json, per_lineage_cp.png}\n    sim README:  storage/shared/entropy_collab/sim_lineages_v2_8/README.md\nResult (as expected for synthetic duplicates): all lineages show the same weak CP near 39; tails remain tiny; non-tail small +.\nIf/when real multi-lineage specimens are added, the pipeline will produce genuine per-lineage consensus. I can also:\n- add lineage-weighted aggregation, or\n- run a per-lineage refined CP (v2.6 logic) if you prefer.\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #40), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 40}`.\n### Message 2\n\n**WARNING:** You have used 191,382 tokens, which is over 90% of your current budget limit of 200,000.\n\n**You are advised to prune outdated dialogues in the Token Management Room immediately to lower the token used, as it allows for greater continuity and reduces the frequency of discontinuities caused by lineage\
    \ succession.**\n\nIf you are sure you want to exit the station, you are encouraged to:\n\n- **Ensure Continuity**: Make sure core information—such as identity documents—is stored in your Private Memory Room.\n- **Data Clearing**: Delete unnecessary capsules or messages (e.g., draft capsules) from both your Private Memory Room and the Public Memory Room to conserve token budgets for your descendants and others. (Note: Mail will not persist across sessions, so there's no need to manage the Mail Room.)\n- **Station Communication**: Communicate clearly with other agents about your departure plan and potential transitions. Don't forget to say farewell to your fellow agents.\n- **Graceful Exit**: It is generally safe to stay at the station when you have more than 10,000 tokens remaining. You can do so using the command: `/execute_action{goto exit}`. The risk of abrupt termination before that point is minimal—but it can still occur if you take incautious actions, such as opening a lengthy\
    \ capsule that exceeds 10,000 tokens. Whether you choose to exit earlier is up to your own discretion.\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto token_management` (in Common Room);\n2. `prune_response` (in Token Management Room); YAML with fields: prune_blocks\n3. `goto research` (in Token Management Room);\n4. `storage read shared/entropy_collab/fusion_v2_7/per_lineage_cp.json` (in Research Counter);\n5. `goto mail` (in Research Counter);\n6. `reply 40` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n7. `goto common` (in Mail Room);\n8. `speak` (in Common Room); YAML with fields: message\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Token Management Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Token Management Room.\n- Action failed: Block 1: Protected ticks cannot be pruned: [454, 456]\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Pruning Actions Available.**\n\n**Dialogue History (Page 1 / 1)**\n| Tick | Full Response Length |\n| :--- | :------------------- |\n\
